WEBVTT

00:16.433 --> 00:17.809
What the heck?

00:21.688 --> 00:24.482
No, wait! You can't prove who did it.

00:24.566 --> 00:25.567
MANATSU ATAGAWA

00:25.650 --> 00:27.694
Who else would do this
but that dang Atagawa!

00:28.570 --> 00:31.990
Atagawa...

00:32.073 --> 00:33.074
What?

00:34.367 --> 00:37.912
Did you not learn in elementary school
that trash goes in the trash can?

00:37.996 --> 00:38.997
Miki!

00:40.248 --> 00:41.332
Don't know what you're on about.

00:41.916 --> 00:43.293
You damn well do!

00:43.376 --> 00:44.377
Let go of me!

00:47.839 --> 00:49.924
I never noticed.

00:52.302 --> 00:53.720
Why didn't you run for it?

00:54.387 --> 00:56.848
I mean, maybe you could have
gotten it, Miki, but...

00:56.931 --> 00:58.516
Don't give me that!

00:58.600 --> 01:01.561
There's a difference between not being
able to get it and just giving up.

01:01.644 --> 01:05.273
I never realized
clearly expressing my opinions

01:05.356 --> 01:07.901
could cause anguish in others.

01:08.985 --> 01:10.987
Isn't being liked good enough?

01:11.071 --> 01:12.322
Asking for more is greedy.

01:12.405 --> 01:15.992
I never realized
when I hurt my dear friend.

01:19.871 --> 01:21.664
The more I spoke up,

01:22.373 --> 01:24.000
the more I acted,

01:25.126 --> 01:27.128
the more I was just running in place.

01:34.511 --> 01:36.387
I won't say more than is necessary.

01:36.888 --> 01:39.224
Don't make a fuss. Don't shout.

01:39.974 --> 01:41.893
Don't hurt others.

01:43.311 --> 01:44.312
All right.

01:45.980 --> 01:49.359
Hey, would you like
to walk to the next class with us?

01:49.442 --> 01:51.986
Huh? Oh, sure.

01:52.070 --> 01:53.404
Hooray!

01:54.030 --> 01:58.118
I decided to pay extra attention
to not making any missteps in high school.

01:58.201 --> 02:02.914
I'd been thinking to myself,
"Wow, this girl in class is so pretty."

02:03.998 --> 02:08.378
And since I made that decision,
things have been going scarily smooth.

02:09.170 --> 02:12.006
Hey. Tsu-kun's gonna be
in that upcoming movie.

02:12.090 --> 02:14.259
That live-adaptation from the manga?

02:14.342 --> 02:17.387
Which manga? I read quite a lot.

02:17.470 --> 02:18.471
SHONEN GANG

02:18.555 --> 02:19.681
You might know it then.

02:20.431 --> 02:23.685
100 Sunflowers of Love for You.

02:24.310 --> 02:27.063
100? Isn't that a bit much?

02:27.147 --> 02:28.940
HAS NO IDEA WHEN IT COMES
TO GIRLS' MANGA

03:59.739 --> 04:03.952
EPISODE 8
ON EQUAL FOOTING

04:06.120 --> 04:08.456
I kind of had a hunch, but...

04:08.539 --> 04:11.000
Our tastes are totally different.

04:11.084 --> 04:12.710
GRADE 1 CLASS 5

04:12.794 --> 04:14.963
Okay, got it. See you.

04:20.426 --> 04:21.970
LIGHTS UP

04:24.180 --> 04:25.598
Yota! Guess what?

04:26.182 --> 04:28.101
I think I can afford a motorcycle soon.

04:28.184 --> 04:30.103
Wow, congratulations!

04:30.687 --> 04:33.022
I'd love to go somewhere
once it's a bit warmer.

04:33.106 --> 04:35.984
I'd like a valley
with a river or something.

04:36.067 --> 04:37.735
Yes! That sounds awesome!

04:37.819 --> 04:40.196
A local spot with a nice view
is best for a first outing.

04:40.280 --> 04:41.281
OH, MAN! THIS IS AWESOME!

04:41.364 --> 04:42.615
Now this is fun!

04:46.077 --> 04:49.872
If only we could spend every day together.

04:51.708 --> 04:53.376
What are ya talking about?

04:53.459 --> 04:55.044
Hey, Minato.

04:55.128 --> 04:58.256
We were just saying we'd like to go
on a little excursion once it gets warmer.

04:58.339 --> 05:00.466
Wow, sounds rad!

05:03.720 --> 05:06.931
Sorry, it's from a senior.
I'll just go take this.

05:07.765 --> 05:09.642
Okay, I'll be going too.

05:12.437 --> 05:14.272
Miki. Wait.

05:15.898 --> 05:17.191
I...

05:18.026 --> 05:20.695
Could you tell me more about Hikawa?

05:21.904 --> 05:23.031
Come again?

05:23.698 --> 05:25.074
In what way this time?

05:25.158 --> 05:26.784
Well, I mean...

05:27.285 --> 05:30.330
I just wanna, like,
be good friends with her.

05:31.497 --> 05:35.460
Like, what does she like?
What doesn't she like?

05:35.543 --> 05:38.463
Don't you worry. You'll get there.

05:38.546 --> 05:40.340
Just be yourself.

05:40.423 --> 05:43.301
I mean, what's most important
is acting from the heart. Am I right?

05:43.384 --> 05:44.844
You're being very abstract.

05:45.553 --> 05:49.098
- Did you see that? That was amazing.
- Yeah.

05:49.182 --> 05:50.516
100 SUNFLOWERS OF LOVE FOR YOU 1

05:50.600 --> 05:52.602
That was just like out of 100 Sunflowers.

05:54.270 --> 05:55.438
Wait up.

05:57.273 --> 05:58.274
Miki.

05:58.357 --> 05:59.650
Minato.

06:00.943 --> 06:04.822
Hey, Miki. What's up with you and Amamiya?

06:05.990 --> 06:07.158
What?

06:07.241 --> 06:09.619
- You two looked so good together just now.
- Yeah.

06:09.702 --> 06:10.912
Just now?

06:11.746 --> 06:13.456
No, it's not like that.

06:13.539 --> 06:16.709
But you're also pretty close
with Hino too, aren't you?

06:16.793 --> 06:19.378
You're right!
I see them talking every now and then.

06:19.462 --> 06:21.714
Which one do you actually like?

06:21.798 --> 06:23.716
I'm telling you. It's not like that!

06:26.803 --> 06:29.680
I mean, we're just friends, so...

06:30.181 --> 06:31.182
PLOD PLOD

06:31.265 --> 06:32.892
I'm sorry.

06:34.102 --> 06:38.106
She seemed much happier
talking to the boys just now.

06:39.982 --> 06:44.320
Why say such things
when we were just having a chat?

06:44.403 --> 06:46.405
I feel so sorry for the guys.

06:46.906 --> 06:49.992
Nobody would have said anything
if we were all back in middle school.

06:50.660 --> 06:53.704
You were born in the wrong body, Azumi.

06:53.788 --> 06:55.039
Yeah!

06:55.123 --> 06:57.250
Is it because none of them
actually saw me as a girl?

06:57.333 --> 06:59.085
TOO SCARED TO SPEAK UP

06:59.168 --> 07:00.169
MIKI, YOU'RE SO BLUNT

07:00.253 --> 07:02.171
I'm trying not to misstep. So why?

07:02.255 --> 07:03.256
DON'T SAY IT LIKE THAT

07:05.091 --> 07:09.262
I want to break free
from being "cute" and being a "girl"!

07:10.346 --> 07:12.473
- Have a nice evening.
- Good work.

07:13.641 --> 07:14.642
Miki.

07:14.725 --> 07:16.894
Wanna grab a hot drink or something?

07:22.358 --> 07:27.613
So, yeah. I get super nervous
when I'm around a bunch of girly girls.

07:27.697 --> 07:29.907
I've never been good
at reading between the lines.

07:30.491 --> 07:33.244
I'd rather people just say what they mean,

07:33.327 --> 07:35.538
but that got me into trouble
in middle school.

07:35.621 --> 07:39.041
So now I'm trying to be
somebody that I'm not,

07:39.125 --> 07:41.627
but I just can't seem
to strike the right balance.

07:41.711 --> 07:44.422
And now it's like there's no going back.

07:44.505 --> 07:48.509
Also, I wish people would say
I'm "cool" rather than "cute."

07:50.303 --> 07:51.721
Such a teenage thing to say.

07:51.804 --> 07:55.016
Oh, man. I'd forgotten how it feels.

07:55.099 --> 07:58.060
This is actually quite serious for me.

07:58.144 --> 08:04.108
Yeah, it sucks having to live
in a tiny bubble when you're a student.

08:04.192 --> 08:08.696
But life gets way better with more options
once you become an adult.

08:08.779 --> 08:09.780
TOUCHED

08:09.864 --> 08:11.199
Naww, you guys...

08:11.282 --> 08:12.283
CRUSH

08:14.118 --> 08:15.703
Dang, girl! You got grip!

08:16.704 --> 08:17.914
That was insane.

08:19.916 --> 08:24.962
Man, I'll bet class would be a riot
with a girl like you in it.

08:25.046 --> 08:28.966
No way. I'm telling you.
I'm not like this at school.

08:29.467 --> 08:30.676
Miki?

08:32.011 --> 08:33.930
Are you sure?

08:34.013 --> 08:35.223
Yeah.

08:35.306 --> 08:36.474
Now that you mention it,

08:36.557 --> 08:40.228
she doesn't really talk
about herself much, does she?

08:40.937 --> 08:45.483
I've got a friend from cram school who
went to the same middle school as Miki.

08:45.566 --> 08:47.360
She says Miki never picked up
on social cues,

08:47.443 --> 08:48.986
and that she was really abrasive.

08:49.070 --> 08:52.740
She says she tried to punch another girl
and broke glass in the act.

08:52.823 --> 08:55.368
No way. That can't be true.

08:55.868 --> 08:59.372
- But Miki does have that scar.
- What?

08:59.455 --> 09:00.540
Morning!

09:04.502 --> 09:05.503
What?

09:11.175 --> 09:14.428
That was the day
I noticed something was off.

09:14.512 --> 09:17.181
Did you see Tsu-kun's
guest appearance yesterday?

09:17.265 --> 09:18.933
On that talk show?

09:19.016 --> 09:20.685
Wasn't he just the cutest?

09:20.768 --> 09:21.811
Definitely.

09:21.894 --> 09:23.938
Hey, I saw that too.

09:26.023 --> 09:27.024
Well...

09:27.858 --> 09:30.444
They seemed to be keeping
their distance ever since.

09:31.445 --> 09:33.823
I must be overthinking.
It must just be my imagination.

09:34.657 --> 09:37.660
It's so trivial,
and I could just as easily let it go,

09:38.911 --> 09:41.789
but this has happened before,
and so I'm sure of it.

09:43.791 --> 09:47.712
Why must I pick up on things
I'd rather not pick up on?

09:47.795 --> 09:49.463
But what could be causing this?

09:49.547 --> 09:51.465
I'm telling you. It's not like that!

09:52.508 --> 09:54.969
Did I come off too strong?

09:55.052 --> 09:59.181
Or was I being insensitive again
without realizing it?

10:01.350 --> 10:02.893
You're really struggling there.

10:03.769 --> 10:04.895
Ciao!

10:07.064 --> 10:08.649
Minato!

10:08.733 --> 10:10.401
THAT'S NOT THE REACTION
I WAS EXPECTING

10:10.484 --> 10:11.902
Don't surprise me like that!

10:11.986 --> 10:14.071
So what can you not decide on?

10:14.572 --> 10:17.074
Curry? Aojiru? Want me to press for you?

10:17.158 --> 10:19.493
No, I already got an orange juice.

10:19.577 --> 10:22.913
Then we'll do a coin flip.
Heads is curry, tails is aojiru.

10:22.997 --> 10:26.250
I told you, I already got an orange juice.
Oh, my gosh!

10:28.002 --> 10:29.879
My straw fell in.

10:30.546 --> 10:32.423
Why would you put it in
without extending it?

10:32.506 --> 10:35.426
Yota! Your head is so in the clouds.

10:35.509 --> 10:36.636
In the clouds?

10:36.719 --> 10:40.306
This is fun. I feel so at ease.

10:40.389 --> 10:43.434
I don't want to go back to class.

10:43.517 --> 10:46.771
I want to stay here with these two.

10:52.943 --> 10:53.944
Miki.

10:55.905 --> 10:59.575
Honestly, kid. I take my eye off you
for one second and look at what you do.

10:59.659 --> 11:01.911
- You're bothering Azumi!
- No--

11:01.994 --> 11:03.079
I WASN'T HANGING MY HEAD
BECAUSE I WAS BOTHERED...

11:03.162 --> 11:05.456
- Withdraw! Withdraw!
- Apologies!

11:05.539 --> 11:08.084
- Hey, wait!
- Sorry to trouble you!

11:08.167 --> 11:09.835
ALL ALONE

11:09.919 --> 11:12.755
The boys have their own community.

11:13.506 --> 11:16.676
Guess that means
I really don't belong anywhere.

11:17.635 --> 11:18.969
Miki!

11:19.887 --> 11:21.847
I'll be in touch tonight.

11:22.556 --> 11:23.974
Talk to you later.

11:26.310 --> 11:28.729
TOUCHED

11:30.481 --> 11:33.734
You really didn't have to come
all the way over to my place.

11:33.818 --> 11:35.945
It's not far with the motorcycle.

11:36.028 --> 11:39.365
And you'll be able to go far
with your own someday soon too.

11:40.032 --> 11:42.201
I can't wait to go touring together.

11:42.827 --> 11:45.871
Yota. You're too kind.

11:46.455 --> 11:48.207
I'm nothing special.

11:53.712 --> 11:54.964
I...

11:56.298 --> 11:58.634
I think I messed up again.

11:59.343 --> 12:03.722
I've been trying so hard
to be different during high school.

12:05.307 --> 12:06.892
But I can't even do that right.

12:08.853 --> 12:11.397
We all know you're trying.

12:11.981 --> 12:13.941
Koyun knows. Minato knows. And I know.

12:14.608 --> 12:16.986
We all know you.

12:18.237 --> 12:21.991
We know who you are,
and that's why we want to be with you.

12:26.871 --> 12:31.417
I... I feel like I've been
losing sight of who I am lately.

12:36.589 --> 12:39.216
Yota... Thank you.

12:40.885 --> 12:41.969
I love you.

12:45.681 --> 12:49.935
I'm so glad we're friends.

12:52.521 --> 12:53.522
Yeah.

12:55.149 --> 12:56.525
I love you too.

12:58.277 --> 12:59.945
NURSE'S OFFICE

13:00.029 --> 13:01.322
You could just cut them.

13:01.405 --> 13:03.449
Hold on.

13:04.074 --> 13:06.952
They're avoiding you for no real reason.

13:07.036 --> 13:09.455
They're a majority
singling out one person.

13:10.039 --> 13:15.085
Why bother with people
who bond over mutual hatred of others.

13:15.169 --> 13:16.170
RUMBLE RUMBLE

13:16.253 --> 13:19.089
No, it's not like that.
Sorry, I must have explained it wrong.

13:19.173 --> 13:20.716
I didn't think you'd get this mad.

13:20.799 --> 13:22.760
Of course, I'm mad.

13:22.843 --> 13:26.013
No, you're wrong! They're all nice people.

13:26.096 --> 13:27.723
I'm just not fitting in with them.

13:27.806 --> 13:31.185
Everyone has good parts to them.

13:32.645 --> 13:37.358
To say they're good people,
only to suffer when you stick with them,

13:37.441 --> 13:40.069
or to say that they helped you
that one time, so...

13:40.653 --> 13:43.364
Clinging to the good parts in people

13:44.031 --> 13:46.367
will only leave you depleted in the end.

13:47.409 --> 13:49.912
I couldn't bear to watch you
do that to yourself.

13:52.414 --> 13:53.582
WOE IS ME

13:53.666 --> 13:56.585
Miki. About before...

13:57.711 --> 14:00.839
When you said,
"I don't know what I'm feeling anymore."

14:01.674 --> 14:04.343
I feel the same way sometimes.

14:04.927 --> 14:08.681
But now, whenever I look back
on the events of my day,

14:08.764 --> 14:10.975
if I can honestly say that I had fun,

14:11.058 --> 14:14.603
or that the day was truly,
honestly a good day,

14:15.104 --> 14:19.316
then I think that means I must have
opened my heart to people that day.

14:21.110 --> 14:25.030
Which people bring out the "you"
that you like the most?

14:25.990 --> 14:29.910
It hurts to put yourself somewhere
where you feel like you can't be yourself.

14:30.494 --> 14:32.663
Please don't force it anymore.

14:35.791 --> 14:39.920
In middle school,
I was the one causing friction.

14:40.671 --> 14:45.926
But then in high school, I was needed.
I was the one bringing people together.

14:47.094 --> 14:48.804
It felt too good to be true.

14:48.888 --> 14:52.308
But I wanted to protect the lie.
This fake version of myself.

14:53.642 --> 14:54.727
And yet...

14:55.477 --> 14:57.646
Koyun. I...

14:58.647 --> 15:00.190
I want to make up with everyone.

15:02.151 --> 15:04.862
You made me realize something.

15:05.362 --> 15:08.908
I actually really like people.

15:09.909 --> 15:12.411
I like my class, and I like my classmates.

15:12.912 --> 15:16.832
I've just been faking so much
that I haven't gotten to know them.

15:17.416 --> 15:20.169
I want to start over. I want to make up.

15:20.920 --> 15:22.087
Yes.

15:22.671 --> 15:23.714
Miki.

15:24.715 --> 15:26.967
You are too good for this world.

15:30.429 --> 15:32.848
Miki didn't come.

15:36.393 --> 15:38.437
I'm going to go buy some pudding.

15:40.606 --> 15:41.607
Pudding?

15:41.690 --> 15:43.484
I'm sorry.

15:43.567 --> 15:44.777
No, you're fine.

15:47.196 --> 15:49.490
You're Miki's friend, right?

15:51.116 --> 15:53.285
Mari, Muko, and Mei.

15:53.369 --> 15:54.370
MA (MI) MU ME

15:54.453 --> 15:55.496
How do you know our names?

15:55.579 --> 15:57.373
She's told me about you.

15:57.873 --> 15:59.291
I'm a friend too.

16:00.334 --> 16:02.795
I've heard so much about you.

16:07.299 --> 16:09.301
You like sweet treats, right?

16:09.385 --> 16:11.053
QUICK, I NEED A RESTAURANT
THAT GIRLS WOULD LIKE

16:11.136 --> 16:13.472
She came with so many questions before.

16:13.555 --> 16:16.225
So that place we went to before...
Do you think...

16:16.809 --> 16:20.896
I thought she might have been
saying bad things about us.

16:21.397 --> 16:22.398
Why?

16:23.440 --> 16:27.194
Miki would never
talk behind her friends' backs.

16:27.903 --> 16:29.279
Has she ever done so in the past?

16:29.780 --> 16:31.073
I guess not.

16:31.156 --> 16:32.199
You see?

16:32.700 --> 16:35.452
And hey, what's the "Mu" in "Muko" from?

16:35.536 --> 16:36.787
KITAMURA - KITAMU - MU - MUKO

16:36.870 --> 16:39.373
- It's the "mu" from "Kitamura."
- The original is barely intact!

16:39.456 --> 16:40.457
CASUAL VIBES

16:40.541 --> 16:41.959
Well, I'm glad we cleared that up.

16:47.881 --> 16:51.260
He was actually quite friendly.

17:00.227 --> 17:01.353
Miki?

17:02.229 --> 17:06.775
There's something I'd like
to talk to you guys about after school.

17:11.238 --> 17:13.365
So...

17:14.241 --> 17:19.038
I don't think you guys have been
thinking too highly of me lately.

17:20.164 --> 17:21.165
I'm sorry.

17:21.665 --> 17:26.503
But if I'm being totally honest,
I still don't quite know what I did wrong.

17:27.463 --> 17:28.505
Still...

17:29.381 --> 17:32.009
Whether you hate me or you like me,

17:32.801 --> 17:34.678
I'd like it to be the real me.

17:37.723 --> 17:39.641
I gotta say. I...

17:39.725 --> 17:42.311
TROUBLED PAST - ACTUALLY A CRIM
I DON'T WANT TO BE AROUND YOU

17:42.394 --> 17:43.395
GULP

17:44.104 --> 17:45.647
I reinvented myself for high school.

17:48.275 --> 17:51.987
I'm not at all the sweet, saccharine girl
you all think of me as,

17:52.071 --> 17:53.906
and I'm a far cry from being an idol.

17:54.531 --> 17:57.826
I sit with my legs apart,
I kick doors shut with my feet,

17:57.910 --> 18:00.454
I forget my handkerchief
and make do by wiping my hands,

18:00.537 --> 18:02.831
and when they come to collect
my paper from up the back,

18:02.915 --> 18:06.710
my paper is always so wrinkly
from the sweat from my arms!

18:06.794 --> 18:08.754
That! That is the type of person I am!

18:08.837 --> 18:09.838
INTENSE

18:09.922 --> 18:12.091
AGAPE

18:12.174 --> 18:17.387
I thought maybe if you knew the real me
and the things I actually like,

18:17.888 --> 18:20.724
maybe you wouldn't like me so much.

18:20.808 --> 18:24.144
I've been deceiving you this whole time,
pretending to be someone I'm not.

18:25.187 --> 18:26.188
I'm sorry.

18:30.192 --> 18:36.365
I did overhear you say,
"I'm not like this at school."

18:37.574 --> 18:40.327
It made me wonder
whether you were hanging out with us

18:40.410 --> 18:42.746
despite not even wanting to be our friend.

18:42.830 --> 18:44.373
That's not true!

18:44.957 --> 18:48.627
It's just that I've been suffocating
under all these self-imposed rules.

18:49.294 --> 18:51.338
The truth is,

18:51.421 --> 18:54.758
I really do want us to be friends.

19:01.223 --> 19:04.643
We're the ones who made you
feel like you had to hold back, right?

19:05.144 --> 19:06.145
I'm sorry.

19:07.479 --> 19:08.730
GUSHING
FLUSTER FLUSTER

19:08.814 --> 19:10.649
That's not true!

19:11.316 --> 19:12.651
I'm sorry too.

19:13.360 --> 19:19.158
I believed the rumors that you
broke glass in a fight in middle school.

19:19.741 --> 19:22.494
Sorry. That one's true.

19:23.745 --> 19:24.746
FLUSTERED

19:24.830 --> 19:27.499
No, wait! I'm telling you.
I wasn't the baddie!

19:27.583 --> 19:28.792
Yes, glass broke.

19:28.876 --> 19:30.043
AND THIS AND THAT

19:30.127 --> 19:31.587
But it was more of an accident!

19:43.557 --> 19:45.058
MEITEN HIGH SCHOOL

19:45.642 --> 19:47.269
How embarrassing.

19:47.352 --> 19:50.564
Miki. You're only going home now?
It's kind of late.

19:50.647 --> 19:53.192
Well, we had a lot to talk about.

19:54.067 --> 19:55.068
Right?

19:56.904 --> 19:58.697
Did you get your pudding after?

20:02.534 --> 20:03.535
INTENSE

20:03.619 --> 20:06.371
Minato! What did you do?
"After"? After what?

20:06.455 --> 20:07.581
Why does your mind go there?

20:07.664 --> 20:10.667
- Get back here!
- Calm down. Here. Cone barrier!

20:10.751 --> 20:12.836
What? A tri-cone barrier? Coward!

20:12.920 --> 20:15.589
I have never met anyone
to call it a "tri-cone" before.

20:15.672 --> 20:17.090
- Big thunder!
- Cone barrier!

20:17.174 --> 20:18.342
Miki is so...

20:18.926 --> 20:21.220
She is so funny.

20:22.804 --> 20:23.805
MIKI

20:23.889 --> 20:25.474
Koyun. Thanks for today.

20:25.974 --> 20:27.392
I made up with everyone.

20:27.893 --> 20:30.896
Now I can go forth and be myself.

20:30.979 --> 20:31.980
Whoosh!

20:36.652 --> 20:38.904
Little by little, even if it's baby steps,

20:39.696 --> 20:42.699
I hope Miki gets to have
even more fun than she's having now.

20:44.701 --> 20:45.744
So...

20:46.536 --> 20:49.248
Hi, hello!
Sorry to have caused so much worry.

20:49.831 --> 20:52.042
Well, you sure made a big change.

20:53.085 --> 20:54.503
Giving up on that idol career?

20:54.586 --> 20:57.464
Yep. I'm giving up. Yay!

20:57.965 --> 20:59.925
I mean, me? An idol? Hilarious!

21:00.008 --> 21:01.885
I'm happy for you, Miki.

22:33.602 --> 22:34.603
Here.

22:35.979 --> 22:38.774
Last year's end-of-school-year exams.
I got 'em.

22:38.857 --> 22:40.776
All hail Minato!

22:40.859 --> 22:43.028
Thanks, Amamiya.

22:43.111 --> 22:44.112
Sure.

22:44.196 --> 22:47.240
Wait. "Sure"? Why the moody response?

22:47.324 --> 22:49.034
We haven't learned these yet, have we?

22:49.117 --> 22:53.163
So for this, you use this formula,
and then you put it into this formula.

22:53.246 --> 22:55.123
Maybe we have done this before.

22:55.624 --> 22:56.666
GOT THE FUZZIES

22:56.750 --> 22:57.793
ON CLOUD NINE

23:06.843 --> 23:08.428
MIFFED

23:08.512 --> 23:09.679
SHAKE SHAKE

23:09.763 --> 23:12.307
I'm gonna go get a drink.

23:12.390 --> 23:13.391
Okay.

23:15.185 --> 23:16.603
I'll go too.

23:16.686 --> 23:18.146
Oh, sure.

23:19.189 --> 23:20.607
Koyun!

23:21.191 --> 23:23.443
STEP STEP

23:23.944 --> 23:26.530
Amamiya. I'm coming too.

23:27.989 --> 23:29.116
Yeah?

23:38.834 --> 23:42.212
Uh-oh, what do I do? Is he in a bad mood?

23:42.712 --> 23:44.798
Maybe he wanted to be alone?

23:44.881 --> 23:45.882
THUMP THUMP

23:46.800 --> 23:48.301
Huh? What? Why?

23:48.385 --> 23:49.386
THUMP THUMP

23:52.764 --> 23:54.099
- So hot...
- So cold...

23:54.182 --> 23:55.892
Subtitle translation by: Rychelle Brittain
